# Nexus.Api domain work

Follow [`docs/architecture-blueprint.md`](docs/architecture-blueprint.md).

## When adding a feature

1. Place code under the correct bounded context (`Accounts`, `Payments`, `Operations`, …)
2. Mutate via Application use case → aggregate → repository port
3. Split by role at the Application/Presentation boundary only
4. Prefer `Ports/In/<Role>/…/I<Action>UseCase` + `UseCases/<Role>/…/<Action>Handler`
5. Keep reads on `I*ReadRepository` / query handlers; writes on aggregate repositories

## Reject these patterns

```csharp
// BAD — god service / role as root capability bag
public interface IAdministrator { /* dozens of methods */ }

// BAD — controller talking to repository or mutating aggregate
public async Task<IActionResult> Refund(string id) =>
    Ok(await _repo.Save(payment.Refund()));
```

```csharp
// GOOD — narrow port + handler returns IOperationResult<T>
public interface IRefundPaymentUseCase
{
    Task<IOperationResult<RefundPaymentResult>> ExecuteAsync(
        RefundPaymentCommand command,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}
```
